# Auto-picked Commons figures. Both figure builders document these caches as the
# thing that keeps image picks stable across builds and hand-overridable, and
# build-geography-figures.js even claims it is "git-tracked via data/". Under the
# blanket `data/*` rule above it was NOT tracked, so the caches were lost on every
# fresh clone and every rebuild silently re-rolled all ~123 unverified figures.
!data/geo-auto-figures.json
!data/subject-figures-cache.json
# Curated figure inputs. The question shards are contaminated (each subject's set
# is a near-complete A-Z Wikipedia sweep), so figure topics are curated from the
# UPSC syllabus by hand in these two files. They must be tracked: the build and
# the GitHub resolver both need them, and they are the only record of which
# figure belongs to which subject. figure-files-curated.json holds hand-picked
# exact Commons filenames (the geography-pack method, always wins);
# figure-files-auto.json is the structured-data resolver's output.
!data/figure-topics-curated.json
!data/figure-files-curated.json
!data/figure-files-auto.json
# mains.html fetches this bank at runtime. slim-live builds its deploy from the
# git index (git write-tree), so an un-allowlisted file here would publish a
# mains page that silently renders nothing.
!data/mains-questions.json
# ask.html fetches this prebuilt retrieval index at runtime. Same reasoning as
# mains-questions.json: slim-live builds from the git index, so without this the
# Ask page would load with no data.
!data/ask-index.json
# Ask's question-bank routing tables. The browser needs these to decide which
# corpus shards a question routes to: the manifest and directory are tiny, the
# entity table is 10.4 MB, and the concept table is measured category evidence.
# The evidence shards themselves (828 MB under data/ask-qb/, ask-qb.*.json) are
# deliberately NOT allowlisted; ask.html treats a 404 on those as "not deployed"
# and falls back to the timeline engine.
!data/ask-qb/
data/ask-qb/ask-qb.*.json
question-bank/
add_entries.js
add_entries_phase2.js
insert_entries.ps1

